{"repositoryId":955764309,"availability":"available","full":"chunlaw/wing-font-generator","name":"wing-font-generator","description":"Generates OpenType fonts that show pronunciation annotations stacked above Chinese characters in plain text ","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":20,"forks":3,"created":"2025-03-27T06:50:00Z","updated":"2026-10-19T05:34:06Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"http://wing-font.chunlaw.io/","topics":["automation","cantonese","font-creation","font-design","font-generator","fonts","hong-kong","ivs","minnan","opentype","opentype-fonts","pinyin","southern-min","svg","taiwanese","teochew","ttf","typography","webfonts","woff"],"demo":"https://wing-font.chunlaw.io/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T06:19:34.047Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T06:19:34.047Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T06:19:34.047Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T19:18:23.758Z","stars":20,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-19T06:19:34.047Z","stars":20,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Bake pronunciation annotations directly into Chinese fonts — Cantonese Jyutping, Mandarin Pinyin, Taiwanese Tâi-lô, and more — so they render in plain text anywhere a custom font goes.","Wing Font generates OpenType fonts whose glyphs carry their own romanization above them. Type 行 and hang4 appears above it; type 銀行 and the same character renders with hong4 because the word-context disambiguation rides on OpenType ccmp. No HTML markup, no separate text layers, no special apps — Word, Pages, Canva, Adobe Creative Cloud, Chrome / Firefox / Safari all just work.","The pipeline is a small Python program that adds GSUB rules to a base CJK font. The same code runs in the browser via Pyodide, so non-developers can compose their own variants without installing anything."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chunlaw/wing-font-generator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"21a8e994e96c1f6b478292878a8d086